// SECOND ALLEN & HEATH MODEL PAGE, and it exists because the equipment graph
// already points at it: the Xone:92 page carries newer: 'xone-96', and both
// /equipment and the Allen & Heath hub render a link to this URL. Until this
// file existed, all three of those were live broken links.
//
// Structure, section order, class names and the style block are lifted from the
// sibling, src/pages/knowledge/allen-heath/xone-92.astro, including its
// dedicated SAFETY group. Facts come from XONE_96 in src/data/facts.js and from
// nowhere else. Every flag, list and source URL is there, so nothing here is
// hard coded that the data layer already holds.
//
// HOW THIS PAGE DIFFERS FROM THE SIBLING, and each difference is a documented
// fact rather than a style choice.
//
// 1. THE MASTER INSERT TRAP LEADS THE PAGE. A jack in MASTER INSERT RETURN
//    breaks the through connection to the master bus, so an outboard unit that
//    is switched off, or a cable somebody left plugged in, kills the master AND
//    the meters. The mixer looks dead and is not. It is the single most
//    valuable fact here and it is quoted in Allen & Heath's own words.
//
// 2. THIS MIXER HAS TWO DOCUMENTED WAYS FOR THE METERS TO DISAGREE WITH THE
//    ROOM. The insert trap is one. The other is that MASTER 1 and MASTER 2 do
//    not move the LR MIX meters at all, so a silent PA with healthy meters is a
//    normal documented state. The two are paired on purpose: a DJ who knows
//    both diagnoses in seconds instead of minutes.
//
// 3. FIRMWARE IS A DIFFERENT CLAIM FROM THE XONE:92's. The 92 has NO firmware.
//    The 96 HAS firmware and Allen & Heath do not publish its history: no
//    version, no date, no change text, and the old v1.0.2 audio firmware pages
//    on their own site now 404. So there is no version for a DJ to check
//    against a list. Rendered from firmwarePublished, and it must never be
//    shortened to "no firmware", which would be the other mixer.
//
// 4. THERE IS NO LFO ON THIS MIXER. The string does not appear in the guide.
//    The Xone:92 has two, so the filters section says so in one sentence,
//    rendered from XONE_92.lfos, because a DJ moving between the two desks will
//    go looking for them.
//
// 5. X:LINK CAN DAMAGE HARDWARE. It is a proprietary Allen & Heath MIDI and PoE
//    protocol and connecting third party gear to it may damage the hardware.
//    That is the only physical damage warning on either Xone page, so it sits
//    in the safety group beside the mains earth.
//
// 6. NO PHONO SHORTING PLUGS. They are documented across the Xone series on the
//    92 page and they are NOT part of this mixer's documentation or its box
//    contents, so they are named as absent rather than carried across.
//
// DVS KEEPS ALLEN & HEATH'S TWO WORDS APART. Traktor Scratch is CERTIFIED, the
// wider list is SUPPORT FOR DVS CONTROL, and Serato is not mentioned by them
// anywhere. Rendered from dvsCertified and dvsSupported so the distinction
// cannot rot into a single list.
const UPDATED = XONE_96.checked;

const schema = {
